    "narrative": "With a heavy emphasis on maximizing stolen base potential and favorable matchups against sub-5.00 xERA arms, **Corbin Carroll** (85.93) leads the charge today. His matchup against Bubba Chandler is prime for production; the combination of a high-efficiency park, an elite spot in the order, and Chandler\u2019s slow delivery significantly bolsters the probability of **Corbin Carroll** swiping a bag. He is joined by **James Wood** (76.27) and **Jose Caballero** (75.78) as our primary anchors. **James Wood** benefits from a stellar 0.425 xwOBA and a generous matchup against Shane Bieber, while **Jose Caballero** utilizes a massive +13% dynamic platoon boost against Anthony Kay to vault into the top tier of our daily rankings.\n\nThe lineup construction prioritizes high-floor performers, which led to a difficult decision regarding the utility slot. **Travis Bazzana** (46.83) was the closest to cracking the starting nine, but he ultimately succumbed to the optimizer\u2019s preference for **Vinnie Pasquantino** (62.65). While **Travis Bazzana** offers a solid profile, the 14% platoon advantage handed to **Vinnie Pasquantino** against Taj Bradley was too significant to ignore in a 5x5 format where marginal efficiency gains dictate weekly outcomes. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** (75.94) remains a strong start despite the presence of Michael King; his platoon edge is simply too potent to bench, even against a tougher arm.\n\nRisk management remains a central theme, as several players\u2014including **Dalton Rushing**, **Josh Naylor**, **Brice Turang**, **Cole Young**, **Seiya Suzuki**, and **Mickey Moniak**\u2014are pending official lineup confirmation. **Dalton Rushing** in particular carries a lowered score of 50.33 due to the projected #9 spot, which creates a volatile floor if he is shifted even lower in the order or if the matchup against Luis Castillo stifles his OBP opportunities. We are monitoring these statuses closely to ensure our pursuit of counting stats isn't derailed by late-scratch scenarios or weather-related disruptions, keeping bench options like **Zach McKinstry** and **Isaac Paredes** on standby should any of our primary starters be omitted from their respective lineups.",
